      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear what you're saying about the \"dynamic\" aspect, but I'm still not feeling 100% confident with that distinction. If I'm reading the US9421732 claims correctly, it covers any modular nanoporous substrate used for thermal regulation in these types of solid-state environments. \n\nThe examiner is going to be very aggressive here. If they decide that \"adaptive thermal conductivity\" is just a natural functional outcome of the substrate described in the 2018 patent, we're stuck. It feels like we're walking a very thin line by claiming the material itself is the novelty when the structural application is clearly documented.\n\nBe honest with me—do you think there's a genuine technical gap there, or are we just trying to find a way to make this work because we've already committed to this angle? I need a realistic assessment of how much weight that \"dynamic\" argument will actually carry against a direct structural similarity.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
